1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,880
Hello, and welcome to Focus on the Arts.

2
00:00:01,880 --> 00:00:06,710
I'm your host - Dave Green - and this is your very own local radio programme.

3
00:00:06,710 --> 00:00:10,508
Every Friday evening we put the spotlight on different arts and culture facilities,

4
00:00:10,508 --> 00:00:14,890
and look at the shows and events that are on offer in the coming week.

5
00:00:14,890 --> 00:00:18,400
And today the focus is on The National Arts Centre.

6
00:00:18,400 --> 00:00:23,000
Now, if you don't already know it yourself, I'm sure you've all heard of it.

7
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:27,430
It's famous throughout the world as one of the major venues for classical music.

8
00:00:27,430 --> 00:00:31,760
But did you know that it is actually much more than just a place to hear concerts?

9
00:00:31,760 --> 00:00:36,630
The Centre itself is a huge complex that caters for a great range of arts.

10
00:00:36,630 --> 00:00:41,794
Under a single roof it houses concert rooms, theatres, cinemas, art galleries

11
00:00:41,794 --> 00:00:44,680
and a wonderful public library

12
00:00:44,680 --> 00:00:48,680
as well as service facilities including three restaurants and a bookshop.

13
00:00:48,680 --> 00:00:53,480
So at any one time, the choice of entertainment there is simply enormous.

14
00:00:53,480 --> 00:00:59,400
So, how did they manage to build such a big arts complex right in the heart of the city?

15
00:00:59,400 --> 00:01:04,650
Well, the area was completely destroyed by bombs during the war in 1940.

16
00:01:04,650 --> 00:01:09,668
So the opportunity was taken to create a cultural centre that would be, what they called:

17
00:01:09,668 --> 00:01:11,550
'the City's gift to the Nation'.

18
00:01:11,550 --> 00:01:15,686
Of course it took a while for such a big project to get started,

19
00:01:15,686 --> 00:01:17,300
but it was planned in the 60s

20
00:01:17,300 --> 00:01:21,300
built in the 70s and eventually opened to the public in 1983.

21
00:01:21,300 --> 00:01:25,100
Ever since then it has proved to be a great success.

22
00:01:25,100 --> 00:01:30,980
It is not privately owned, like many arts centres, but is still in public hands

23
00:01:31,420 --> 00:01:32,620
it's run by the City Council.

24
00:01:32,620 --> 00:01:35,540
Both our National Symphony Orchestra

25
00:01:35,540 --> 00:01:38,375
and National Theatre Company were involved in the planning of the project,

26
00:01:38,375 --> 00:01:42,098
and they are now based there - giving regular performances every week -

27
00:01:42,098 --> 00:01:46,340
and as the Centre is open 363 days of the year

28
00:01:46,340 --> 00:01:48,530
there are plenty of performances to choose from.

29
00:01:48,530 --> 00:01:51,254
So, to give you some idea of what's on,

30
00:01:51,254 --> 00:01:53,860
and to help you choose from the many possibilities

31
00:01:53,860 --> 00:01:56,400
we've made a selection of the star attractions.

32
00:01:56,400 --> 00:01:58,504
If you're interested in classical music,

33
00:01:58,504 --> 00:02:04,320
then we recommend you go along to the National on either Monday or Tuesday evening at 7

34
00:02:04,320 --> 00:02:07,624
30 for a spectacular production of 'The Magic Flute' -

35
00:02:07,624 --> 00:02:10,430
probably the most popular of all Mozart's operas.

36
00:02:10,430 --> 00:02:13,481
It's in the Garden Hall and tickets start at only £8.00,

37
00:02:13,481 --> 00:02:17,040
but you'll have to be early if you want to get them that cheap!

38
00:02:17,040 --> 00:02:20,400
And remember, it's only on for those two evenings.

39
00:02:20,400 --> 00:02:22,578
For those more interested in the cinema,

40
00:02:22,578 --> 00:02:25,360
you might like to see the new Canadian film

41
00:02:25,360 --> 00:02:28,800
which is showing on Wednesday evening at 8pm in Cinema 2.

42
00:02:28,800 --> 00:02:30,683
And that's called 'Three Lives.'

43
00:02:30,683 --> 00:02:34,800
It's had fantastic reviews and tickets cost just £4

44
00:02:34,800 --> 00:02:38,590
50, which is a reduction on the usual price of £5.50.

45
00:02:38,590 --> 00:02:42,400
So, it's really good value, especially for such a great movie.

46
00:02:42,400 --> 00:02:46,060
But you can see the centre's main attraction at the weekend

47
00:02:46,060 --> 00:02:49,517
because on Saturday and Sunday, 11 am to 10 pm,

48
00:02:49,517 --> 00:02:54,600
they're showing a wonderful new exhibition that hasn't been seen anywhere else in Europe yet.

49
00:02:54,600 --> 00:02:59,805
It's a collection of Chinese Art called 'Faces of China' - that's in Gallery 1 -

50
00:02:59,805 --> 00:03:03,720
and it has some really fascinating paintings

51
00:03:03,720 --> 00:03:05,755
and sculptures by leading artists from all over China -

52
00:03:05,755 --> 00:03:10,960
and the good news is that it is completely free, so don't miss it!

53
00:03:10,960 --> 00:03:15,440
So why not go along to the National Arts Centre next week for one

54
00:03:15,440 --> 00:03:17,066
or all - of these great events -

55
00:03:17,066 --> 00:03:22,867
and you can always pick up a programme and check out all the other performances and exhibitions on offer,

56
00:03:22,867 --> 00:03:25,920
or coming soon, on almost every day of the year.

57
00:03:25,920 --> 00:03:29,800
Next week we'll be looking at the new Museum of Science...
